[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1751","stub":{"id":"1751","section":"2. Apalachia Powerhouse to Reliance ","altname":"","river":"Hiwassee","difficulty":"II","states":["USA-TNN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"stale","latestReading":{"value":"17.88","dateTime":"2018-06-05T14:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"The powerhouse put-in (river right) has a concrete ramp, ample parking, and toilet.  Forest Service day use fee required.","id":"108295","location":{"latitude":"35.1806","longitude":"-84.4435"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"playspot","description":"Soon after the mouth of Towee Creek (on river right) the river descends over a short series of ledges, before being diveded by Cane Island. Work to the left, taking the left channel. This chute is in turn divided by a rock jumble. Go to the left or to the right.","id":"2254","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Thread the Needle","distance":"1.6","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"access","description":"As the river works around Big Bend, it approaches a 3 foot drop, most prominent on river left--Mary Nell Point. On river right, before the drop is the Big Bend Parking area.","id":"2253","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Mary Nell Point","distance":"2.1","photoID":"12899","difficulty":"II","approximate":false},{"type":"playspot","description":"A series of ledge drops that last well over a quarter mile -- one of the common lines is to start river right and work over to river left.","id":"2251","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Stairstep Rapid","distance":"2.5","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"12898"},{"type":"playspot","description":"As you approach the island, take the river left channel -- this line involves a short series of Class 2+ ledge drops","id":"2252","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Little Rock Island","distance":"3.1","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"playspot","description":"As the river bends to right, there are another series of shallow ledge drops. Soon the river is divided by Big Island. The most common line is to take the river right channel. The channel drops over a 2-3 foot ledge with three chutes. An excellent place to catch eddies and to suff.","id":"2255","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Funnel Rapid","distance":"4","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"882023"},{"type":"playspot","description":"Continue down the left channel around Big Island. The channel widens and then begins to both drop over another series of ledges, as the channel constricts. The fast current and turbulent water form Devil's Shoals. As you work down the ledges, there are eddies that can be caught on the right. As you work down the rapid, a ledge appears on river left, work down the center of the channel for this last section.","id":"2256","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Devil's Shoals","distance":"4.6","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"50973"},{"type":"takeout","description":"Take out on river left just downstream of the railroad bridge at the state park access area.  Concrete ramp, ample parking, toilet.  In the summer, a ride to the top is available at adjacent Hiwassee Outfitters for $5 - buses leave on the hour.","id":"113538","location":{"latitude":"35.188058","longitude":"-84.499527"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"5.6","photoID":"38kQXC0jv9dSDxP9AcumK","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"874669","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"874670","description":"Matt Todhunter surfing the bottom of stairsteps.","caption":"Surfing the bottom of stairsteps","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.o