This five mile plus section offers several playful Class II rapids, and with its width, the opportunity for many lines. For the most part, the best water is near river left and on the left channels around the islands.\n\nIn addition to the internet link for the TVA above, one may obtain the predicted release for the following day by calling the TVA flow number: 800-238-2264 (toll-free) then pressing 4, then 22, and then the # sign. If you call on a Friday (after 6pm) then you can obtain the release predictions for Saturday and Sunday.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"5.6","correlations":[{"reachID":"1751","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"15","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"30"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"HIWASSEE RIVER AT CHARLESTON, TN","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"03566000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ARCHIVED","latestFlowReading":{"value":"10300","dateTime":"2018-06-05T13:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"17.88","dateTime":"2018-06-05T14:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"35.29514804","longitude":"-84.759955"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/03566000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/03566000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 15 - 30 levelFT  Comment: See the TVA Appalachia Dam release schedule. Flows can change hourly.\n\nMigration Errors: \nSingle range is valid but doesn't provide low/medium/high runnable\nThere is one comment for all of low/medium/high ru